From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:16:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: reset: Add the resets of the Glymur USB4 host
 routers

A Glymur USB4 host router controls two things for the PCIe root complex
it tunnels into: the hold on its side of the pipe interface, and
PERST#, which it passes down the tunnel. Name them, so that the root
complex can take them as resets from the router.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 include/dt-bindings/reset/qcom,glymur-usb4.h | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 include/dt-bindings/reset/qcom,glymur-usb4.h

diff --git a/include/dt-bindings/reset/qcom,glymur-usb4.h b/include/dt-bindings/reset/qcom,glymur-usb4.h
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..7c4bee775
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/dt-bindings/reset/qcom,glymur-usb4.h
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause) */
+/*
+ * Resets a Qualcomm Glymur USB4 host router provides to the PCIe root
+ * complex whose tunnel it carries.
+ */
+
+#ifndef _DT_BINDINGS_RESET_QCOM_GLYMUR_USB4_H
+#define _DT_BINDINGS_RESET_QCOM_GLYMUR_USB4_H
+
+/* Holds the router's side of the root complex's pipe interface. */
+#define QCOM_GLYMUR_USB4_PCIE_PIPE	0
+/* PERST# of the tunnelled link, passed on by the router. */
+#define QCOM_GLYMUR_USB4_PCIE_PERST	1
+
+#endif
-- 
